Startup shader loader. Applied by installer/tools/assemble_payload.py to the payload's copy of the toolkit; the checked-out
repository is not edited.
Every guest-FP pipeline a run builds is noted in game\run\shadercache\pipelines.bin (description plus VS/PS bytecode). At the
first guest-FP draw of the next run all noted pipelines are built once on several threads ("Preparing shaders n/N" in the window
title) and released, so the driver already has them when the game asks: no menu or HUD pieces skipped for frames while
pipelines build (a tester's GTX 1080 showed an empty main menu on its second start). The first run of an install has nothing to
warm up. PSO_WARMUP=0 turns it off; it follows SHADER_CACHE.
Tested on Windows 11 (RTX 5080 Laptop): run 1 "no pipelines noted yet", 232 pipelines noted (5.4 MB) through the menus and a
fight; run 2 "warmed 232 of 232 noted pipelines in 0.1 s on 8 thread(s)", main menu complete.
